Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:45:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/21] dtb: treat a self-parented interrupt controller as a
 root

The OnePlus 6 DTB names the GIC as the root interrupt-parent and gives the
GIC its own maintenance PPI, so the GIC recorded a parent link to itself.
No controller below it was initialised: TLMM, PDC and the architected timer
translation all failed. Linux of_irq_init treats a controller whose parent
is itself as a root; do the same, and log the TLMM->PDC->GIC wake route
when a userspace IRQ claims it.

